ty cardboard box is light enough to hold with one hand.","opposite":"heavy","illustrationKey":"light","entryType":"vocabulary","senseLabel":"not heavy"},{"id":"thick","category":"condition-state","word":"thick","ipa":"/θɪk/","pos":"adj.","definition":"large in depth or thickness","sentence":"The encyclopedia is a very thick hardcover book.","opposite":"thin","illustrationKey":"thick","entryType":"vocabulary"},{"id":"thin","category":"condition-state","word":"thin","ipa":"/θɪn/","pos":"adj.","definition":"having little thickness or depth","sentence":"This thin notepad slips easily into your pocket.","opposite":"thick","illustrationKey":"thin","entryType":"vocabulary"},{"id":"sharp","category":"condition-state","word":"sharp","ipa":"/ʃɑːp/","pos":"adj.","definition":"having a thin edge or fine point","sentence":"A sharp pencil point makes drawing precise lines easy.","opposite":"blunt","illustrationKey":"sharp","entryType":"vocabulary"},{"id":"blunt","category":"condition-state","word":"blunt","ipa":"/blʌnt/","pos":"adj.","definition":"having a dull, flat edge or point","sentence":"The pencil tip has worn down blunt and needs sharpening.","opposite":"sharp","illustrationKey":"blunt","entryType":"vocabulary"},{"id":"clear","category":"condition-state","word":"clear","ipa":"/klɪər/","pos":"adj.","definition":"sharp, detailed, and easy to see","sentence":"The high-definition camera captured a clear tree photo.","opposite":"blurry","illustrationKey":"clear","entryType":"vocabulary"},{"id":"blurry","category":"condition-state","word":"blurry","ipa":"/ˈblɜːri/","pos":"adj.","definition":"unfocused, indistinct, or fuzzy","sentence":"Without glasses, distant objects look quite blurry.","opposite":"clear","illustrationKey":"blurry","entryType":"vocabulary"},{"id":"charged","category":"condition-state","word":"charged","ipa":"/tʃɑːdʒd/","pos":"adj.","definition":"holding full electrical energy","sentence":"My phone is 100% charged with three green bars.","opposite":"dead","illu